  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Sustainable and responsible enterprises in Pakistan promoted</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">The proposed strategy for the years 2024-2025 endeavors to empower SMEs, steering them towards a future characterized by sustainability and responsibility. This will include fostering an eco system that can enable SMEs just transition to formalisation, access to finance, technology and initiatives that can help environmental sustainability and market access.
Guided by the principles of the International Labour Organization&apos;s Tripartite Declaration, the strategy places emphasis on embedding fair wages, safe working conditions, and skill development opportunities at the core of responsible business conduct. Consequently, supply chains will evolve into conduits that promote decent work instead of exploitation, fostering respect not only within large corporations but also across the intricate network of SMEs. 
The strategy will also include promoting productivity through ILO approaches including Sustainable Competitive Responsive Enterprises, Factory Improvement Tool, Workplace Improvement for Sustainable Enterprises among others.
Training programs, designed to equip entrepreneurs with new skills, innovation, and technology, act as bridges connecting businesses to green practices. This holistic approach aims to propel productivity, nurture sustainable practices, and unlock the true potential of the informal sector, catalyzing a paradigm shift in the way SMEs operate. 
Further value chains are mapped to identify livelihood opportunities for vulnerable groups including migrant workers and refugees, based on the analysis, selected value chains are developed to enable sustainable decent living for vulnerable groups.
The sectoral focus for the CO is based on export potential, existing trade preferential schemes and sectors where climate change , technological advancement, demographics have negatively  impacted sustainability and working conditions. Addressing these concerns from a lens of ensuring Just transitions, upskilling and environmental sustainability.</narrative>
  </description>
